<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 September, from 617 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">617 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,409 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Li Yuan defeats a Sui army at Huoyi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The rebel Duke of Tang, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang">Li Yuan</a>, advancing on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> capital, routed an elite Sui army of 20,000 at Huoyi after an initial setback. The victory opened his path to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> and the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang">Emperor Gaozu of Tang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1198">1198 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">828 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philip of Swabia is crowned German king at Mainz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> Cathedral, Archbishop Aymon II of Tarentaise, not the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> as was usual, crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-swabia">Philip of Swabia</a> King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Elected by the Staufen party while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welfs</a> chose Otto IV, Philip faced a long civil war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-swabia">Philip of Swabia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1380">1380 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">646 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dmitry of Moscow defeats Mamai at Kulikovo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On Kulikovo Field near the upper Don, an army of Russian principalities led by Grand Prince Dmitry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> defeated the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamai">Mamai</a>, warlord of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>. The victory earned Dmitry the name Donskoy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kulikovo">Battle of Kulikovo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1504">1504 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">522 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Michelangelo's David is unveiled in Florence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a>'s colossal marble <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> was unveiled outside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-vecchio">Palazzo Vecchio</a>. Carved from a block other sculptors had abandoned, it became a symbol of the Florentine Republic.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1565">1565 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">461 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Ottomans abandon the Great Siege of Malta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After nearly four months, the Ottoman army withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a>, defeated by the Knights of St John under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-parisot-de-valette">Jean de Valette</a>. The new capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valletta">Valletta</a>, was named after him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1664">1664 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">362 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Dutch hand New Amsterdam to the English</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Facing English warships and an unwilling population, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-stuyvesant">Peter Stuyvesant</a> surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a> without a fight. It was renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> after the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">York</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy's armistice with the Allies is announced</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> broadcast news of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s surrender. German troops quickly disarmed the Italian army and occupied much of the country, which became a battleground for 20 months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1974">1974 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gerald Ford pardons Richard Nixon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Ford granted Nixon a full pardon for any crimes he 'committed or may have committed' in office. Ford said it would end the national ordeal; it damaged his own popularity.</p></div></li></ol>
