<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 8 September <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leo-iv-the-khazar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leo-iv-the-khazar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leo IV the Khazar</span><span class="tp">750–780</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-navarre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-iii-of-navarre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles III of Navarre</span><span class="tp">1361–1425</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-quevedo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francisco-de-quevedo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francisco de Quevedo</span><span class="tp">1580–1645</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maria-carolina-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maria-carolina-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maria Carolina of Austria</span><span class="tp">1752–1814</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adam-opel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adam-opel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adam Opel</span><span class="tp">1837–1895</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/faisal-i-of-iraq"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/faisal-i-of-iraq.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Faisal I of Iraq</span><span class="tp">1885–1933</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elizabeth-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Elizabeth II</span><span class="tp">1926–2022</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
